      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would rather not. The cast is required either way: with the union, `export const AUTO_MERGE: ParentPatchSet \u003d \u0027AUTO_MERGE\u0027;` still fails with `Type \u0027\"AUTO_MERGE\"\u0027 is not assignable to type \u0027ParentPatchSet\u0027`, because a plain literal does not satisfy the brand. So the union does not remove anything, it only widens a type that is part of the plugin API to claim that the REST API accepts `AUTO_MERGE`, which it never does: it is normalized to `PARENT` in `computeBase()` before any request is made. I can move the constant out of `api/rest-api.ts` into `types/common.ts` if you prefer to keep it away from the plugin API entirely.",
