      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T08:42:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One question regarding non-merge commits:\n\nWhat happens if a user navigates to a URL containing `0` or `auto-merge` on a normal, non-merge (single parent) commit (e.g. via an outdated or shared link)? Does the change model/router fallback cleanly to `PARENT` without erroring when requesting auto-merge from the backend?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "6930855cd7ddaf253451b0ea52442024ebb6dd03",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "892502fc_5b20e6ef",
        "filename": "polygerrit-ui/app/elements/core/gr-router/gr-router.ts",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 452,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T08:53:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it falls back to `PARENT` cleanly, and no auto-merge request ever reaches the backend.\n\n`auto-merge` never appears in a URL — only `0`, which the router maps to `AUTO_MERGE` in the view model. `computeBase()` returns `PARENT` for `AUTO_MERGE` unconditionally, as its very first check, without ever looking at whether the commit is a merge. Both views read `basePatchNum$` from the change model, so the REST API only ever sees `PARENT`. The next navigation also drops the `0` from the URL, because `urlBasePatchNum()` only emits it when the preference would pick a different base.",
      "parentUuid": "b9f16483_2698b191",
      "revId": "6930855cd7ddaf253451b0ea52442024ebb6dd03",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
